      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "6677ec40-f6fc-5f61-ab08-119b4ad52a11",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Geoffrey S. Fletcher, Saoirse Ronan, Alexis Bledel, Marianne Jean-Baptiste, Danny Trejo, James Gandolfini, Julio DePietro, Scott Porter, Bryan Greenberg, Dante Di Loreto\n- Films: Violet & Daisy, Precious, The Good Guy, Temple Grandin, The Normal Heart\n- TV Series: The Handmaid's Tale\n- Awards: Academy Award for Best Adapted Screenplay, Primetime Emmy Award\n- Topics: acting roles, directorial debut\n\nFacts:\n- In 2009, Julio DePietro directed the romantic comedy film The Good Guy, which starred Alexis Bledel, Scott Porter, and Bryan Greenberg.\n- In 2011, Violet & Daisy was released as an American comedy crime drama film written, produced, and directed by Geoffrey S. Fletcher in his directorial debut.\n- Before making Violet & Daisy, Geoffrey S. Fletcher won the Academy Award for Best Adapted Screenplay for Precious.\n- Violet & Daisy starred Saoirse Ronan, Alexis Bledel, Marianne Jean-Baptiste, Danny Trejo, and James Gandolfini.\n- James Gandolfini's role in Violet & Daisy was one of his last acting roles before his death on June 19, 2013.\n- Alexis Bledel was born on September 16, 1981, and she is an American actress and model.\n- Alexis Bledel won a Primetime Emmy Award for her work on the Hulu drama series The Handmaid's Tale.\n- Dante Di Loreto is a two-time Primetime Emmy Award winner for his work on Temple Grandin and The Normal Heart.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "1c9958ba-4f61-596f-bc7b-1e3a9c65cfa0",
        "text": "Page: Violet &amp; Daisy. Sentence: Violet & Daisy is a 2011 American comedy crime drama film written, produced, and directed by Geoffrey S. Fletcher in his directorial debut after winning an Oscar for Best Adapted Screenplay for the film Precious.\nPage: Violet &amp; Daisy. Sentence: The film stars Saoirse Ronan, Alexis Bledel, Marianne Jean-Baptiste, Danny Trejo, and James Gandolfini in one of his last acting roles before his death on June 19, 2013.\nPage: Alexis Bledel. Sentence: Kimberly Alexis Bledel ( ; ] ; born September 16, 1981) is an American actress and model.\nPage: Alexis Bledel. Sentence: She won a Primetime Emmy Award for her work on the Hulu drama series \"The Handmaid's Tale\".\nPage: The Good Guy (film). Sentence: The Good Guy is a 2009 romantic comedy film directed by Julio DePietro starring Alexis Bledel, Scott Porter, and Bryan Greenberg.\nPage: Dante Di Loreto. Sentence: He is a two-time Primetime Emmy Award winner and for his work on \"Temple Grandin\" and \"The Normal Heart\".",
